# GitHub PR File Explorer Enhancer

Chrome extension that adds navigation and review helpers on GitHub pull request **Files changed** pages (`/pull/<number>/files`).

## Install

**Requirements:** Node.js 18+, Chrome (or another Chromium browser). Git optional if you download the repo as a ZIP.

```bash
git clone <repo-url> pr-file-explorer
cd pr-file-explorer
npm install
npm run build
```

Then load the built extension:

1. Open `chrome://extensions`.
2. Turn on **Developer mode**.
3. Click **Load unpacked** and choose this project’s **`dist/`** folder (not the repo root).

**Pin the icon:** Extensions menu (puzzle piece) → find **GitHub PR File Explorer Enhancer** → pin it so the popup stays one click away.

For a slower, step-by-step guide (ZIP download, troubleshooting), use [INSTALL.md](INSTALL.md).

**Updates:** After pulling new changes, run `npm run build` again and click **Reload** on the extension card in `chrome://extensions`.

## Start using it

1. Open any GitHub PR and go to the **Files changed** tab.
2. Keep the PR **file tree** visible if you want **locate in explorer** to scroll and highlight the matching file.
3. Click the **extension icon** in the toolbar to turn features on or off and adjust back-to-top clicks.
4. Optional: **Extension options** — `chrome://extensions` → this extension → **Extension options** — for editor command settings (`cursor` / `code`) and local repo root.

First time you use the **terminal-style “open in editor” control** on a file header, you’ll be prompted for editor choice and your local clone path. You can change that anytime from the options page or via Option-click on that button (see [INSTALL.md](INSTALL.md)).

## Features

### Toolbar popup

- Toggle **locate file in explorer** (per-file header button).
- Toggle **IDE-like file tabs** above the diff.
- Toggle **review-flow rail** and each rail action individually (previous/next comment, next unviewed file, copy context, copy comments for agents).
- Toggle the **floating back-to-top** button.
- Choose what a normal click vs **Shift+click** does for back-to-top: jump to **top of Files** or **top of page**, and swap the two with one control.

### On the PR page

- **Locate:** Icon on each file header scrolls the sidebar tree to that file and flashes it.
- **Back to top:** Floating control after you scroll; respects your click / Shift+click settings from the popup.
- **File tabs:** Single-click a file header for an italic **preview** tab; double-click the header or tab (or use the pin control) to keep a **permanent** tab; click tabs to jump between files.
- **Review rail:** Jump comments, next unviewed file, copy Markdown review context, copy unresolved threads for agents; shows status for the current file’s comments.
- **Comment dots:** Subtle markers in the file tree for files that have visible review threads.

### Options page

- Enable or disable the **editor command copy** feature, pick **Cursor** vs **VS Code**, and set **local repo root** so copied commands look like `cursor -g "/path/to/repo/file.ts:line"`.

---

## For developers

```bash
npm install          # once
npm run dev          # HMR; outputs to dist/
npm run build        # production build
npm run typecheck    # TypeScript only
```

**Stack:** TypeScript, Vite, Manifest V3 (`@crxjs/vite-plugin`), vanilla DOM on GitHub pages, React + Tailwind popup and options UI.

**Docs:** [Requirements](docs/requirements.md), [DOM map](docs/dom-map.md), [Implementation plan](docs/implementation-plan.md).

**Legacy:** A Tampermonkey-style script still lives at `src/github-pr-file-explorer.user.js` for non-extension users; the extension build uses the TypeScript content script.
